{"name":"Concrete Jungle","hex":"#999988","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"concrete jungle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An urban or other populated area containing a high density of buildings constructed of concrete or similar materials, especially one which lacks greenery and which seems unattractive, harsh, or unsafe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concrete_jungle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Concrete Jungle (David \"Fathead\" Newman album)","blocks":[{"text":"Concrete Jungle is an album by American jazz saxophonist David \"Fathead\" Newman recorded in 1977 and released on the Prestige label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/48/Concrete_Jungle_%28David_Fathead_Newman_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concrete_Jungle_(David_%22Fathead%22_Newman_album)"},{"title":"Concrete Jungle (The OST)","blocks":[{"text":"Concrete Jungle [The OST] is the first compilation album by American heavy metal band Bad Omens, released on May 31, 2024 through Sumerian Records. The album is considered a follow–up to the record, The Death of Peace of Mind. It also serves as the companion soundtrack to the graphic novel \"Bad Omens – Concrete Jungle, Volume 1\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f1/Bad_Omens_Concrete_Jungle_THE_OST_Album_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concrete_Jungle_(The_OST)"},{"title":"Concrete","blocks":[{"text":"Concrete is a composite material composed of aggregate bound together with a fluid cement that cures to a solid. It is the second-most-used substance, the most widely used building material, and the most-manufactured material in the world. Cement-bound concrete differs from the less rigid, less durable asphaltic concrete, which has a bituminous binder."}],"image":"https://thumb.